From ec863d0ac0de72435a535cf5c7ba2b863f145ff0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hc-push <hc-push@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:44:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gossip): request a gossip round with a verified peer

Add an additive Gossip::request_round(url) API (default: unsupported) and
implement it in K2Gossip. A requested peer must be a live agent in the peer
store, so its signed agent info was verified on insert. The initiate task
tries requested peers first, retries transient failures (e.g. the local
relay is not registered yet right after start-up) up to 10 times, and then
falls back to ordinary target selection. Forced initiations now also end the
wait while the storage arc is growing and after the fetch queue drained.

Responder-side rate limiting (burst tracking) is unchanged.
